            <ArticleTitle>[Observation on therapeutic effect of acupuncture on no-premonitory migraine at remission stage].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>679-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To observe therapeutic effect of acupuncture on no-premonitory migraine at remission stage.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The scores of pain extent, attack times, lasting time and accompanied symptoms of headache were investigated before treatment and after treatment of 4 weeks.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">After treatment of 4 weeks, the scores of all items had significant changes (P &lt; 0.01). The total effective rate was 95.0%.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Acupuncture has obvious analgesic effect on no-premonitory migraine at remission stage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
